  "hints": [
    "With prefix sums P, the subarray (i, j] has sum P[j] - P[i]. So you need pairs i < j with P[j] - P[i] = k.",
    "That is a two-sum on the prefix sums: for each j count earlier prefixes equal to P[j] - k.",
    "Keep a hash map prefix value -> occurrences, initialised with {0: 1} for the empty prefix. For each element update the running sum, add map[sum - k], then insert sum."
  ],
  "editorial": "Let `P[0] = 0` and `P[j] = a[1] + ... + a[j]`. A subarray `(i, j]` has sum `P[j] - P[i]`, so we count pairs `i < j` with `P[i] = P[j] - k`. Sweep `j` and maintain a map from prefix value to the number of earlier prefixes (including the empty prefix `P[0] = 0`, which is why the map starts with `{0: 1}`).\n\nThis works with negative numbers because it never relies on monotonic prefix sums. Expected `O(n)`. The answer can be about `n^2/2` (all zeros, `k = 0`), so use 64-bit counters; prefix sums reach `n · 10^9`, which also needs 64 bits.",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n)",
    "space": "O(n)"
  },
  "starter": {
    "python": "import sys\n# prefix sums + hash map\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\n# your code here\n",
    "javascript": "// prefix sums + hash map\n// readLine() returns the next input line (or null).\n// your code here\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    // prefix sums + hash map\n    return 0;\n}\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        // prefix sums + hash map\n    }\n}\n"
  },
  "solutions": {
    "python": "import sys\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\nn, k = int(data[0]), int(data[1])\ncnt = {0: 1}\ns = 0\nans = 0\nfor x in map(int, data[2:2+n]):\n    s += x\n    ans += cnt.get(s - k, 0)\n    cnt[s] = cnt.get(s, 0) + 1\nprint(ans)\n",
    "javascript": "const [n, k] = readLine().trim().split(/\\s+/).map(Number);\nconst a = readLine().trim().split(/\\s+/).map(Number);\nconst cnt = new Map();\ncnt.set(0, 1);\nlet s = 0, ans = 0;\nfor (const x of a) {\n  s += x;\n  ans += cnt.get(s - k) || 0;\n  cnt.set(s, (cnt.get(s) || 0) + 1);\n}\nconsole.log(String(ans));\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        StreamTokenizer in = new StreamTokenizer(new BufferedInputStream(System.in));\n        in.nextToken();\n        int n = (int) in.nval;\n        in.nextToken();\n        long k = (long) in.nval;\n        HashMap<Long, Integer> cnt = new HashMap<>();\n        cnt.put(0L, 1);\n        long s = 0, ans = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            in.nextToken();\n            s += (long) in.nval;\n            ans += cnt.getOrDefault(s - k, 0);\n            cnt.merge(s, 1, Integer::sum);\n        }\n        System.out.println(ans);\n    }\n}\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    long long k;\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    map<long long, int> cnt;\n    cnt[0] = 1;\n    long long s = 0, ans = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        long long x;\n        cin >> x;\n        s += x;\n        auto it = cnt.find(s - k);\n        if (it != cnt.end()) ans += it->second;\n        cnt[s]++;\n    }\n    cout << ans << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n"
  }
